@CLS@@X0DPACK/RENUMBER MESSAGES

@X0EPack the Message Base?
@X0D<@X0EN@X0D>@X0E  Do not pack the message base.  Return to the conference command prompt.
@X0D<@X0EY@X0D>@X0E  Pack the message base.  Additional questions will be asked to determine
     the criteria you want to use. (if any)

Generate ONLY a New Index File?
@X0D<@X0EN@X0D>@X0E  If you enter this response, additional questions will be asked to
     determine the criteria for deleting messages.
@X0D<@X0EY@X0D>@X0E  No additional questions.  PCBPack will run and create a new message base.
     Good idea if you think a message base may be corrupt.

Purge older than?
Enter the cutoff date for keeping messages.  Any messages older than this date
will be deleted.   The default entry of 010180 will not delete any messages.

Purge RECEIVED+PRIVATE Msgs?
@X0D<@X0EN@X0D>@X0E  Leaves any RECEIVER ONLY messages in the data base.
@X0D<@X0EY@X0D>@X0E  All RECEIVER ONLY messages that have been read will be deleted.



Renumber during repack?
@X0D<@X0EN@X0D>@X0E  Do not renumber the message base -- Message numbers will stay the same.
@X0D<@X0EY@X0D>@X0E  The message base will be renumbered beginning with the number you will be
     asked to specify.  When the message base is renumbered, the last message
     read values will NOT be updated.
@X07
